ion/math-academy-id "q-125739" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=yz-x.$ Calculate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is any smooth path from $(-1,2,0)$ to $(-2,3,1)$ in ${R}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nIn our case, the coordinates of the endpoints of the path $C$ are $A(-1,2,0)$ and $B(-2,3,1).$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r & =f(-2,3,1)-f(-1,2,0) \\\\  & =(3(1)-(-2))-(2(0)-(-1)) \\\\  & =5-1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-125739/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5598fb5a-b749-56ec-8b86-49d73206b58c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125739"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125732/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "60584d50-ae9c-57f8-a9d4-84852394e31e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125732/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "22e5cd49-7d51-5f61-bb06-83a24cb55df7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125732/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "e5d4f95d-cc18-5d95-b4cb-831945ee1ccf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125732/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "4da07cff-4385-539c-8819-a5b6c787aeda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125732/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "aec21ea0-8f7c-5681-9514-095ebc24f248" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125732/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2277dfee-6c19-55fa-a71e-d0998091124c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125732/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-125732/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-125732/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-125732/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" "q-125732/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-125732/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125732" :question/id #uuid "57187fd1-9c5a-5946-8baf-39d008054731" :question/math-academy-id "q-125732" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Calculate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is any smooth path from $(-\\pi ,0)$ to $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ in ${R}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nIn our case, the coordinates of the endpoints of the path $C$ are $A(-\\pi ,0)$ and $B(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r & =f(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})-f(-\\pi ,0) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =(1-1)-(0+1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125732/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5598fb5a-b749-56ec-8b86-49d73206b58c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125732"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125735/selection/c63183ecc9d835663ee418360ec9fafbce922f11e8c31cee35e8cd30e6afa971" :answer/id #uuid "7a2aec7f-e628-5455-bb6a-17903d707dc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125735/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "8713fdaa-469f-55ed-a3da-e9a13151c1a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125735/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "64f66f4b-2313-5fe7-8460-9a37747bc01a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125735/selection/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" :answer/id #uuid "8606daaa-3216-5e22-b6b2-81002cb18605" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125735/selection/6273a1ce826479f6324c67b6111789f3a2ae7f61836a9bf7e56848eb8a1214e1" :answer/id #uuid "ce28ad11-ee78-5b2f-aadb-dfd8e9cf6c7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125735/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b42c53a-d9e9-58a0-9452-af9d17b1060b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125735/selection/6273a1ce826479f6324c67b6111789f3a2ae7f61836a9bf7e56848eb8a1214e1" :answer-field/choices ["q-125735/selection/c63183ecc9d835663ee418360ec9fafbce922f11e8c31cee35e8cd30e6afa971" "q-125735/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-125735/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-125735/selection/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" "q-125735/selection/6273a1ce826479f6324c67b6111789f3a2ae7f61836a9bf7e56848eb8a1214e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125735" :question/id #uuid "d6e1f75d-d8f3-5ced-ae66-51b7d4322a8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-125735" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+1}.$ Calculate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is any smooth path from $(-2,1)$ to $(0,3)$ in ${R}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nIn our case, the coordinates of the endpoints of the path $C$ are $A(-2,1)$ and $B(0,3).$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r & =f(0,3)-f(-2,1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{{0}^{2}+1}-\\frac{1}{(-2)^{2}+1} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125735/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5598fb5a-b749-56ec-8b86-49d73206b58c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125735"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125737/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "387bfb64-3564-55b2-9027-ae3274fe3130" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125737/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "f09491bf-deae-5311-bd35-a62559c7962b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125737/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "11bed988-c157-560a-917d-3fc85d34b075" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125737/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "3de9079c-1a94-5d29-a46a-98b903a32b69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125737/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0e740ad0-4dcf-5dd3-9dc7-04608a8ceb6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125737/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd1c738-0d3a-5256-a7a1-3f22fc308a1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125737/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-125737/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-125737/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-125737/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-125737/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-125737/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125737" :question/id #uuid "e0cb0760-74e6-5697-8e4e-c8fe0c3b2e54" :question/math-academy-id "q-125737" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y,z)={x}^{3}-{y}^{2}+z.$ Calculate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is any smooth path from $(1,0,3)$ to $(0,-1,2)$ in ${R}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nIn our case, the coordinates of the endpoints of the path $C$ are $A(1,0,3)$ and $B(0,-1,2).$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r & =f(0,-1,2)-f(1,0,3) \\\\  & =({0}^{3}-(-1)^{2}+2)-({1}^{3}-{0}^{2}+3) \\\\  & =1-4 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-125737/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5598fb5a-b749-56ec-8b86-49d73206b58c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125737"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125726/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "4a5276ef-9283-5b98-9d0c-02b65198581f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125